{
  "schemaVersion": "autov.lab/2",
  "name": "Energy overload column",
  "description": "A golden energy column erupting out of a plain dark machine cylinder on a bare stage. Over the first 1.5 s the column intensifies from a low glow into a 4.5 m segmented shaft — a white-gold core inside a tapered orange-gold shell inside a hard-tiered slab — wrapped in a cage of white-blue arcs that blink on their own short cycles. At 1.5 s it erupts: a lens flare opens at head height, a clumped fan of orange, pink and pale-gold streaks throws outward, sparks and dark chips fly ballistically, a thin shock ring snaps out and a near white-out washes the frame at 1.85 s. The eruption holds to 3.5 s, then one shared collapse retracts the whole column from the top and narrows it until only a dim glow over the cylinder is left.",
